WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.890
Sometimes a number is not enough.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:08.290
In this video you will add a photo, a short
video and a sensor reading to a measurement,

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.762
and then find them on your list.

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:13.479
Open Add a measurement.

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.943
Type a few letters of your station's name, and
it appears in the list.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.718
Round buttons appear.

00:00:20.838 --> 00:00:23.478
Each one adds something to your visit.

00:00:23.598 --> 00:00:28.566
Three are for this video: Photo, Video and
Scan for sensors.

00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.495
Type the main number first.

00:00:31.615 --> 00:00:34.855
Here the water is twelve point four metres
down.

00:00:35.683 --> 00:00:38.755
Press Photo, and a photo box opens.

00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:43.075
A picture of the well or the gauge shows the
next person what you saw.

00:00:43.883 --> 00:00:47.171
On a phone, Take photo opens the camera.

00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:50.459
Take your picture, and it comes straight back
here.

00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:56.611
Choose from device picks a picture you already
have, from your gallery or your files.

00:00:56.731 --> 00:00:58.603
We choose one now.

00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:03.161
Here is the preview, with the file name and
size.

00:01:03.281 --> 00:01:05.681
It is sent only when you save.

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:11.427
Add a short caption if you like, such as:
Water level in the well today.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.170
Chose the wrong picture?

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:16.882
Press Remove, and pick another.

00:01:17.002 --> 00:01:21.010
The Photo button now shows a one: your photo
is ready.

00:01:21.817 --> 00:01:23.689
Now Video.

00:01:23.809 --> 00:01:29.305
A short video shows what a photo cannot, like
water flowing, or the sound of a pump.

00:01:30.117 --> 00:01:32.973
Record video opens the phone camera.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.285
Choose video picks a clip you already have.

00:01:36.405 --> 00:01:40.965
A clip can last ten seconds; a longer one
keeps its first ten.

00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:44.687
OurWater now makes the video smaller.

00:01:44.807 --> 00:01:46.799
Watch the number climb.

00:01:46.919 --> 00:01:50.423
It takes about as long as the clip, so please
wait.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.122
Why?

00:01:53.242 --> 00:01:57.658
A phone video can be huge, and a weak signal
might never send it.

00:01:57.778 --> 00:02:00.370
A small video uploads fast.

00:02:01.183 --> 00:02:03.487
Here is your smaller video.

00:02:03.607 --> 00:02:05.479
Press play to watch it.

00:02:05.599 --> 00:02:07.471
The sound is kept.

00:02:07.591 --> 00:02:10.111
Its size is shown underneath.

00:02:10.917 --> 00:02:12.789
Not happy with it?

00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:16.629
Press Remove video, then record or choose
another.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:23.906
The last button is Scan for sensors, for a Bluetooth
water pen: a small meter that you dip in the water.

00:02:24.717 --> 00:02:27.381
Switch the pen on and keep it close.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:31.509
Press the button, and OurWater starts looking
for the pen.

00:02:32.317 --> 00:02:35.557
It connects by itself, and LIVE appears.

00:02:35.677 --> 00:02:42.469
The numbers move while the pen settles: pH,
conductivity, dissolved solids, ORP,

00:02:42.589 --> 00:02:44.533
chlorine and temperature.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.734
This works best on a phone with the OurWater
app.

00:02:48.854 --> 00:02:52.622
On a computer you need Chrome or Edge with
Bluetooth on.

00:02:52.742 --> 00:02:55.526
Here a practice pen shows how it looks.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:59.638
When the numbers are steady, press Hold
values.

00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:04.054
They freeze, and a message says how many boxes
were filled in.

00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:08.099
Temperature and Water quality are now filled
in.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:11.675
Check them; you can change any number by hand.

00:03:11.795 --> 00:03:13.715
Nothing is saved yet.

00:03:14.517 --> 00:03:16.389
Everything is ready.

00:03:16.509 --> 00:03:18.405
Press Save measurement.

00:03:19.217 --> 00:03:21.473
OurWater opens your list.

00:03:21.593 --> 00:03:25.505
This visit is at the top, one row for each
number.

00:03:26.317 --> 00:03:28.693
The small picture is your photo.

00:03:28.813 --> 00:03:31.381
Every row of this visit carries it.

00:03:32.183 --> 00:03:35.591
Beside it, the round play button is your
video.

00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:40.953
Press it, and the video opens big and plays,
with its sound.

00:03:41.073 --> 00:03:44.385
Press Close, or Escape, when you are done.

00:03:45.217 --> 00:03:49.009
The photo also has its own row, with your
caption.

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:53.041
Now anyone who opens this station can see what
you saw.

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:57.882
That is how you add a photo, a video or a
sensor reading.

00:03:58.002 --> 00:04:00.666
Thanks for helping look after our water.
